    "breadcrumb": "Swing Catalyst Palaikymas \u003e Kameros ir vaizdo įrašas",
    "content": "Yra problema su USB tvarkykle licencijų donglams, kuriuos naudoja Halcon klientai. Šis dongas yra žalias USB “Flexera” dongas.\nTvarkyklės, įdiegtos su Halcon 12, sukelia Windows klaidą ir mėlynąjį ekraną.\nNorėdami išvengti mėlyno ekrano, rekomenduojame pašalinti senus tvarkykles, jei jos įdiegtos, išinstaliavus Halcon arba rankiniu būdu pašalinus tvarkykles.\nPaveikia:\nWindows 10 versija 2004 versija \u003e= 19041.423, 20H2, 21H1 arba 21H2\nWindows 11.\nRekomenduojame išinstaliuoti Halcon ir tada vadovautis šiame palaikymo straipsnyje pateiktomis instrukcijomis, kaip įdiegti naują tvarkyklę.\nHalcon išinstalavimas Atverkite Programų ir funkcijų langą.\nDalyje Programos ir funkcijos ieškokite “halcon”.\nSpustelėkite gautą sąrašo elementą ir spustelėkite “Išinstaliuoti” bei “Išinstaliuoti”\nSpustelėkite “Taip”, norėdami tęsti Halcon išinstalavimą, palaukite, kol pradedamas Halcon deinstalatoriaus darbas, tada spustelėkite “Išinstaliuoti”, norėdami pašalinti Halcon.\nAlternative Option: Removing the Halcon USB dongle drivers manually This option can be used if you don’t want to reboot the computer or for some reason don’t want to reinstall Halcon. For most purposes it’s best to follow the “Uninstallign Halcon” option instead.\nWhen a driver is installed it is stored in the Windows DriverStore file repository, located in:\nC:\\Windows\\System32\\DriverStore\\FileRepository\nNormally to remove the driver you would go to Device Manager and uninstall the device \u0026 select to delete the driver, but since plugging in the USB dongle crashes Windows we need to remove it manually. Windows will find the appropriate (new) driver once we install the new driver.\nHow to remove a device driver using pnputil The instructions below uses “quotes” around text that should be typed into the command line without quotes.\nOpen Command Prompt.\nIn Command Prompt, type “pnputil -e” to list all installed drivers.\nLook for drivers at the beginning of the output that has the package name containing Sentinel HASP or SafeNet.\nRemove each of them by running “pnputil /delete-driver drivername.inf /uninstall”\nExample to remove the driver with the publisher name oem53.inf type: “pnputil /delete-driver oem53.inf /uninstall” and hit enter.\nPlease note that the output from pnputil in this case is from a working system that has the updated driver (missing screenshot of old drivers).\nFor a non working system it would should list similar drivers but with a different driver package provider\nInstalling new Halcon USB license dongle drivers The instructions below uses “quotes” around text that should be typed into the command line without quotes.\nDownload and extract the new driver, right click on the downloaded zip file and click “Extract All” \u0026 “Extract”.\nOpen Command Prompt (if you closed it from earlier)\nCopy the location of the extracted driver folder, e.g. C:\\Users\\stian\\Downloads\\haspdinst_8.53\nIn Command Prompt, type “cd” and paste the location of the extracted driver, e.g. “cd C:\\Users\\stian\\Downloads\\haspdinst_8.53”\nType “haspdinst.exe /install” into the Command Prompt then hit enter.\nInstall should proceed.\nLast updated: 2024-06-03 | View on official support site",
    "description": "Šią parinktį galite naudoti, jei nenorite perkrauti kompiuterio arba dėl kokios nors priežasties nenorite iš naujo įdiegti Halcon. Daugumoje atvejų geriausia yra laikytis...",
