    "breadcrumb": "Swing Catalyst Palaikymas \u003e Kameros ir vaizdo įrašas",
    "content": "Rekomenduojami USB 3.0 aukšto greičio kamerų komponentai Labai rekomenduojame USB 3.0 PCI Express korteles darbalaukio sistemoms.\nDauguma integruotų USB 3.0 valdiklių nėra pakankami dideliam pralaidumui / aukštos skiriamosios gebos USB kameroms. Dėl to tai gali sukelti kadro praradimą ir kitus nestabilumo reiškinius). Nuo to nerekomenduojame daugiau nei 1 kamerą nešiojamiems kompiuteriams.\nIntegruoti USB 3.0 valdikliai veikia, bet našumas labai skiriasi priklausomai nuo čipseto, kamerų pralaidumo reikalavimų ir iš viso naudojamų kamerų skaičiaus.\nFaktinis mūsų rekomendacijų ir kamerų našumas gali skirtis.\nTai reiškia, kad viena kamera iš Point Grey gali turėti geresnį našumą su konkrečiu čipsetu, palyginti su viena iš Ximea, arba priešingai.\nTodėl rekomenduojame jums tiesiogiai su mumis susisiekti arba vadovautis kamerų gamintojo patarimu dėl USB 3.0 komponentų.\nRekomenduojami šeimininkų valdikliai ir integruoti čipsetai Išoriniai USB 3.0 valdikliai\nRenesas uPD720202\nRenesas uPD70200A\nFresco FL1009\nFresco FL11100\nFresco FL1100EX\nLSI FW643\nVidiniai čipsetai (nešiojami kompiuteriai / motininės plokštės):\nIntel 7 serija (Ivy Bridge), C216 (HM76) (maks. 451 MB/s)\nIntel 8 serija (Haswell).\nIntel 9 serija (Broadwell).\nIntel 100 serija (Skylake).\nIntel Z87 (Intel 8 Series / C220) Express Chipset (maks. 471 MB/s)\nIntel Q77 Express Chipset\nPlease see: https://www.flir.com/support-center/iis/machine-vision/application-note/recommended-usb-3.1-system-components/ for more detailed information on which motherboards \u0026 laptops that use these chipsets.\nPlease note that actual performance may vary greatly, and that we do not recommend USB 3.0 HD cameras to be used with laptops in general.\nThe maximum USB 3 speed is 500MB/s, but in reality the limit is much lower than this. In many cases the actual performance is about half and in some cases worse than that. This means not all chipsets can handle multiple camera’s with max framerate and resolution.\nTip: Using AOI/ROI (region of interest) can help lower the overall bandwidth usage.\nFor multiple camera setups, e.g two camera setup it’s important each camera uses approx half of max bandwidth to able to use two cameras.\nWarning Some issues have been seen with AMD 300-Series chipsets (AMD Ryzen 1700 / 2700 series ) with USB 1.1 devices. Specifically with the Balance Plate, where you only get 75 samples per second instead of ~145 samples per second. We recommend using a USB 2.0 hub which will allow the Balance Plate to stream at full sample rate.\nThere are no known issues as far as using the AMD 300 series chipsets with USB 3.0 devices.\nRecommended USB 3.0 Cables: Although the USB 3.0 standard does not specify a maximum cable length, we do not recommend cables longer than 3 meters.\nSome 5 meter cables work, whereas others don’t depending on the manufacturer and camera. We recommend to use 3 meter cables + an active USB extension or repeater that fits the USB 3 specification.\nRecommended cable type: USB 3.0 (A to Micro B with locking screws) recommended by your camera manufacturer. The black FLIR 3 \u0026 5 meter USB 3 cables are good alternatives, please contact sales for more information.\nAlternatives: https://www.newnex.com/usb-3-locking-cables.php\nUS2-AMCBI1-3M (3 meter model)\nUS226AMCBI1-5M (5 meter model)\nFor cable lengths longer than 3 meters: It’s important these cables are designed for Machine Vision, and that they are certified for USB3 Vision / Machine Vision by the manufacturer, your average USB extender will not work adequately for this use case.\nWhen needing cable lengths above 5 meters the best solution is to use an extender that uses fiber.\nActive cables use amplification to work around the problem of signal loss and can work in some cases but we recommend to use the shortest cable possible, the better solution is to use fiber extenders, although usually much more expensive, it is the only way to reliably extend USB3 over larger distances.\nActive Cables:\nActive USB 3.0 repeaters (or repeater cables) from Newnex: http://newnex.com/usb3_active_extension.php\nhttps://www.newnex.com/usb-3-active-cable-a-to-micro-b.php Repeater \u0026 extender solutions:\nAlternatives by Newnex and Icron, two manufacturer that deliver Machine Vision compliant cabling:\nhttps://www.newnex.com/firenex-ulink-ds-usb-3-active-repeater.php\nhttps://www.icron.com/products/icron-brand/usb-extenders/cat5/usb-3-0-spectra-3001-15/\nFor longer cable runs fiber repeaters are really the only way you can extend a high frequency high bandwidth signal such as USB3 over longer distances:\nhttps://www.newnex.com/usb-3-extenders.php\nhttps://www.icron.com/products/icron-brand/usb-extenders/ Last updated: 2021-08-05 | View on official support site",
    "description": "Labai rekomenduojame USB 3.0 PCI Express korteles stalinėms sistemoms.",
